IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc30-forms-search.l4 -- FORM 1, 2, 4, 5, 5.1, 5.2 and 5.3 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (raw text lines 17451-17497 and 17911-17945):
-- the Forms used to obtain and execute a search warrant, and the information and the heading of an indictment.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- WHAT IS A RULE HERE. A Form's identification blocks, recitals ("the informant says ..."), signature lines and commands to officers are the
-- prescribed wording of a document and carry no rule of their own (the rule is in the section that prescribes the Form: its part owns it).
-- What this module encodes is what the Forms say beyond their wording: the two Notes on the date of birth (Forms 2 and 4), the notice that tells
-- the person searched what may be done with the things seized and how to get a copy of the report (Form 5.1), and what the report to a justice
-- must attach or state (Form 5.2). How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered).
-- Every JUST FALSE branch carries a FALSE-kind comment that quotes the words; every NOTHING branch carries a NOTHING-kind comment.

§ `Form 2 and Form 4 -- the Note on the date of birth`

-- Note: The date of birth of the accused may be mentioned on the information or indictment. (The same Note ends Form 2 and Form 4.)
-- The grant is limited by its own wording: it names the information and the indictment. Any other document is outside the limit.
-- src:17469 | Note: The date of birth of the accused may be mentioned on the information or indictment.
@ref Form 2 (Sections 506 and 788) Note (src:17469)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 2 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `an information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an indictment` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the information or indictment"

-- src:17487 | Note: The date of birth of the accused may be mentioned on the information or indictment.
@ref Form 4 (Sections 566, 566.1, 580 and 591) Note (src:17487)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 4 note the date of birth of the accused may be mentioned` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `an information` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an indictment` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the information or indictment"

§ `Form 5.1 -- Notice of execution of a search warrant`

-- "If anything is seized during the execution of the warrant, the things that were seized may be brought before the court at (address)."
-- A "may" limited by its "If": when nothing was seized the sentence does not apply and is silent (NOTHING, fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
-- src:17913 | If anything is seized during the execution of the warrant, the things that were seized may be brought before the court at (address). However, if the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant filed with that court a report on the things that were seized, you may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court. The report will indicate the things that were seized and the location at which they are being held.
@ref Form 5.1 (Subsection 320.29(5) and subparagraphs 462.32(4)(a)(ii) and 487.093(1)(a)(ii)) Notice, first sentence (src:17913)
GIVEN `anything is seized during the execution of the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.1 the things that were seized may be brought before the court` MEANS
    IF `anything is seized during the execution of the warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If anything is seized during the execution of the warrant"

-- "However, if the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant filed with that court a report on the things that
-- were seized, you may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court." The person searched holds the liberty; the text states no
-- duty on the clerk (see the Jural relations table in NOTES.md).
-- src:17913 | If anything is seized during the execution of the warrant, the things that were seized may be brought before the court at (address). However, if the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant filed with that court a report on the things that were seized, you may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court. The report will indicate the things that were seized and the location at which they are being held.
@ref Form 5.1 (Subsection 320.29(5) and subparagraphs 462.32(4)(a)(ii) and 487.093(1)(a)(ii)) Notice, second sentence (src:17913)
GIVEN `the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant filed with that court a report on the things that were seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.1 the person may obtain a copy of the report from the clerk of that court` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant filed with that court a report on the things that were seized`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the peace officer, public officer or other person who executed the warrant filed with that court a report on the things that were seized"

§ `Form 5.2 -- Report to a justice: what is said of each thing seized`

-- For each thing seized the report states "whether it was returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, in which case the receipt
-- for it shall be attached to this report; or it is being detained to be dealt with according to law, in which case indicate the location and
-- manner in which or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained."
-- "in which case" is read as "where" (a marginal reading for a lawyer, NOTES.md): when the thing was not returned, the receipt limb does not apply.
-- src:17923 | Thing Seized(describe each thing seized) | Disposition(state, in respect of each thing seized, whetherit was returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, in which case the receipt for it shall be attached to this report; orit is being detained to be dealt with according to law, in which case indicate the location and manner in which or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained.)
@ref Form 5.2 (Subsection 489.1(3)) Report to a Justice, table of things seized (src:17923)
GIVEN `the thing seized was returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.2 the receipt for the thing seized shall be attached to the report` MEANS
    IF `the thing seized was returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case the receipt for it shall be attached to this report"

-- src:17923 | Thing Seized(describe each thing seized) | Disposition(state, in respect of each thing seized, whetherit was returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, in which case the receipt for it shall be attached to this report; orit is being detained to be dealt with according to law, in which case indicate the location and manner in which or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained.)
@ref Form 5.2 (Subsection 489.1(3)) Report to a Justice, table of things seized (src:17923)
GIVEN `the thing seized is being detained to be dealt with according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.2 the location and manner of the detention shall be indicated in the report` MEANS
    IF `the thing seized is being detained to be dealt with according to law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in which case indicate the location and manner in which or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained"

-- "or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained": the person is named only if the thing is being detained AND a person is detaining it.
-- src:17923 | Thing Seized(describe each thing seized) | Disposition(state, in respect of each thing seized, whetherit was returned to the person lawfully entitled to its possession, in which case the receipt for it shall be attached to this report; orit is being detained to be dealt with according to law, in which case indicate the location and manner in which or, if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained.)
@ref Form 5.2 (Subsection 489.1(3)) Report to a Justice, table of things seized (src:17923)
GIVEN `the thing seized is being detained to be dealt with according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a person is detaining the thing seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.2 the person by whom the thing seized is being detained shall be indicated in the report` MEANS
    IF `the thing seized is being detained to be dealt with according to law` AND `a person is detaining the thing seized`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if applicable, the person by whom it is being detained"
